{
  "id": "ep034",
  "duration": 48.382,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.627,
      "text": "Three men are the only humans to have ever died in space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Soviet Union 1971 CPA 4060 stamp (Cosmonauts Georgy Dobrovolsky, Vladislav Volkov and Viktor Patsayev).jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Soviet_Union_1971_CPA_4060_stamp_(Cosmonauts_Georgy_Dobrovolsky,_Vladislav_Volkov_and_Viktor_Patsayev).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.627,
      "end": 10.722,
      "text": "Most people assume space fatalities happened during fiery rocket launches or high-altitude explosions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Soyuz TMA-11M rocket launches from Baikonur (2).jpg",
        "credit": "Bill Ingalls",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soyuz_TMA-11M_rocket_launches_from_Baikonur_(2).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.633,
          "end": 10.733,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.722,
      "end": 19.242,
      "text": "In June 1971, Soyuz 11 launched carrying Georgy Dobrovolsky, Vladislav Volkov, and Viktor Patsayev.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1979 CPA 5027.jpg",
        "credit": "Post of Soviet Union",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1979_CPA_5027.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.733,
          "end": 14.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.667,
          "end": 19.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.242,
      "end": 25.512,
      "text": "The crew successfully docked with Salyut 1, setting new space endurance records over three weeks.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1972 CPA 4112.jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1972_CPA_4112.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.233,
          "end": 25.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.512,
      "end": 30.982,
      "text": "As their capsule separated from the service module prior to re-entry, disaster struck.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Expedition 59 Soyuz MS-11 Landing (NHQ201906250017).jpg",
        "credit": "Bill Ingalls",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Expedition_59_Soyuz_MS-11_Landing_(NHQ201906250017).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 28.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.233,
          "end": 30.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.982,
      "end": 36.932,
      "text": "An equalization valve jarred open, venting all cabin air into the vacuum of space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.967,
          "end": 36.933,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.932,
      "end": 42.602,
      "text": "Because they were not wearing pressurized suits, the three men suffered fatal asphyxiation.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Sokol K space suit (MMA 2011) (1).JPG",
        "credit": "Armael",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sokol_K_space_suit_(MMA_2011)_(1).JPG"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.933,
          "end": 42.6,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.602,
      "end": 48.032,
      "text": "Recovery forces opened the landed capsule to find those three men dead in their seats.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Soviet Union 1971 CPA 4060 stamp (Cosmonauts Georgy Dobrovolsky, Vladislav Volkov and Viktor Patsayev).jpg",
        "credit": "USSR Post",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Soviet_Union_1971_CPA_4060_stamp_(Cosmonauts_Georgy_Dobrovolsky,_Vladislav_Volkov_and_Viktor_Patsayev).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 48.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
